It does.  MR and half-spell-damage reduce the damage taken by half and
the maxHP drain by half.  They do not stack, so having both doesn't
improve things.

> Possibly that he's thought about what I discussed above :) Given that
> Sporkhack also adds in monsters with sickness attacks at low levels,
> I don't know if it can really be classified as "fluffy bunny," even if
> this change does aid the early player.

This change doesn't aid the early player significantly at all.  Things
that can cast 'touch of death' just do not show up frequently enough in
the early game to be worth consideration, fear, or anything else.

Early-game characters chase MR to protect from polytraps and the wands
of death, magic missile, and striking, not arch-liches.

> In general, Nethack could stand to burn up player resources more between
> the Castle and the Planes; making Max HP something that can go _down_ if
> you're not paying attention or burning resources on high-level casters is
> certainly one way to do that.

Correct.  ;)

> Leaving this largely aside, it's worth pointing out that draining maxHP
> will even cut into uber-pumped characters a little bit; 900HP behemoths
